## Ceremonies

We work on a fortnightly cadence. Our ceremonies give us time to agree
priorities, make progress visible and improve how we work together.

| Ceremony | Occurrence | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Stand-up | Monday to Thursday | Share progress, raise blockers and agree what needs a follow-up conversation. |
| Backlog refinement | Fortnightly | Make upcoming work clear enough to discuss and plan. |
| Planning | Fortnightly | Agree the work we will focus on in the next fortnight. |
| Retrospective | Last Friday | Reflect on how we worked and choose improvements to try. |
| Show and tell | Last Thursday | Share progress and learning with colleagues and interested people. |

Stand-up is for coordination, not a status performance. Keep updates brief and
move detailed problem-solving to a follow-up conversation.

Before refinement, read the work likely to be discussed and bring questions.
Work is ready to plan when people understand the outcome, the important risks
and what needs to be true for it to be complete.

Retrospectives look at how we work, what works well, and how we can remove friction.

Show and tell is where we show progress openly for external stakeholders to come and see.